(ned ROTARY FACING -- stock prep. Skim a bar down to a target diameter.)
(Operator 2026-08-12: tool number, starting D, end D, and a length.)

(START AT G55 X0 Y0. Both are checked and the cycle refuses otherwise. That)
(is what lets the operator give ONE positive number for the cut instead of a)
(start and an end -- the datum is the start, and LENGTH runs +Y from it.)

(DIAMETER IS Z. On the centreline the tool tip contacts the crown and nothing)
(else, so tip at Z = D/2 IS diameter D. X is never commanded.)

(THE TOOL COMPENSATION IS IN Y. The tool bottom is a disc: sweeping its)
(CENTRE from 0 to LENGTH actually machines -R to LENGTH+R. To finish exactly)
(between the two edges, the centre runs R to LENGTH-R. A length shorter than)
(the tool is refused rather than fudged.)

(Y FEED IS COMPUTED, NOT ACCEPTED. One turn of B advances Y by one pitch, so)
(Y speed and B speed are the same fact twice. B tops out at 30 deg/s, capping)
(Y at pitch times 30 over 360 times 60 mm/min -- 63 mm/min for a 12.7 tool at)
(full pitch. Taking a bigger number would only mean LinuxCNC clamps B behind)
(the operator's back. Chip load replaces this later.)

(D START IS A PROMISE, NOT A MEASUREMENT. Nothing here can see the stock, so)
(an optimistic number buries the tool on the first pass.)
o<rotary_face> sub
  #<rf_tool>   = #1 (=0 tool number - required)
  #<rf_dstart> = #2 (=0 stock diameter now mm - required)
  #<rf_dend>   = #3 (=0 target diameter mm - required)
  #<rf_len>    = #4 (=0 length to face, +Y from zero - required)
  #<rf_doc>    = #5 (=1.0 radial depth per pass mm)
  #<rf_rpm>    = #6 (=9000 spindle rpm)
  #<rf_step>   = #7 (=0.5 pitch as a fraction of tool diameter)
  #<rf_bmax>   = #8 (=30.0 B max deg/s - JOINT_6 MAX_VELOCITY)
  o1 if [#<rf_doc> LE 0]
    #<rf_doc> = 1.0
  o1 endif
  o2 if [#<rf_rpm> LE 0]
    #<rf_rpm> = 9000
  o2 endif
  o3 if [#<rf_step> LE 0]
    #<rf_step> = 0.5
  o3 endif
  o4 if [#<rf_bmax> LE 0]
    #<rf_bmax> = 30.0
  o4 endif
  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: switch to MM first)
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#<rf_tool> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: no tool number given)
  o11 endif
  o12 if [#<rf_dstart> LE 0 OR #<rf_dend> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: both start and end diameter are required)
  o12 endif
  o13 if [#<rf_dend> GE #<rf_dstart>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: end diameter must be SMALLER than the start diameter)
  o13 endif
  o14 if [#<rf_len> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: length must be positive - it runs +Y from zero)
  o14 endif

  (IN THE RIGHT FRAME FIRST. X0 and Y0 in G54 are somewhere else entirely, so)
  (the position checks below mean nothing without this one. 1 is G54, 2 G55.)
  o15 if [#5220 NE 2]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: not in G55 - the rotary datum lives there, G54 is scratch)
  o15 endif
  (X AND Y BOTH ZEROED. X is never commanded, so a wrong X is never corrected)
  (- it just quietly cuts the wrong thing. The failure this catches is being a)
  (long way out: the air offset is 1000 mm and G54 is 3.67 m away. 0.1 mm is)
  (deliberately loose, because depth error off centre is only dX squared over)
  (2r -- half a mm off a 19 mm radius costs 7 microns.)
  o16 if [ABS[#5420] GT 0.1]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: X is not zeroed - it reads #5420 and must be 0)
  o16 endif
  o17 if [ABS[#5421] GT 0.1]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: Y is not zeroed - it reads #5421 and must be 0)
  o17 endif

  T#<rf_tool> M6
  G43
  o20 if [#5400 NE #<rf_tool>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: the spindle is not holding the tool that was asked for)
  o20 endif
  #<tdia> = #5410
  o21 if [#<tdia> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: that tool has no diameter in the table)
  o21 endif
  #<trad> = [#<tdia> / 2.0]

  #<ya> = #<trad>
  #<yb> = [#<rf_len> - #<trad>]
  o22 if [#<yb> LE #<ya>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: that length is shorter than the tool - nothing to sweep)
  o22 endif

  #<pitch> = [#<tdia> * #<rf_step>]
  #<feed>  = [#<pitch> * #<rf_bmax> * 60.0 / 360.0]
  #<zsafe> = [[#<rf_dstart> / 2.0] + 10.0]
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: T#<rf_tool> dia #<tdia>, pitch #<pitch> mm/rev, Y feed #<feed> mm/min)
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: facing 0 to #<rf_len> - tool centre sweeps #<ya> to #<yb>)

  G90
  G1 G53 Z0 F2000
  M3 S#<rf_rpm>
  G0 Z[#<zsafe>]
  G0 Y[#<ya>]
  G0 B0

  #<d> = #<rf_dstart>
  #<pass> = 0
  o100 while [#<d> GT #<rf_dend>]
    #<d> = [#<d> - #<rf_doc>]
    o101 if [#<d> LT #<rf_dend>]
      #<d> = #<rf_dend>
    o101 endif
    #<pass> = [#<pass> + 1]
    #<z> = [#<d> / 2.0]
    (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: pass #<pass> to diameter #<d>, Z #<z>)
    G0 Y[#<ya>]
    G0 Z[#<z> + 2.0]
    G1 Z[#<z>] F[#<feed>]
    (ONE STEP PER 10 DEG OF B: fine enough not to facet the helix, coarse)
    (enough that a 100 mm pass is not thousands of blocks.)
    #<len>   = [#<yb> - #<ya>]
    #<revs>  = [#<len> / #<pitch>]
    #<steps> = [FIX[#<revs> * 36.0] + 1]
    #<dy>    = [#<len> / #<steps>]
    #<db>    = [#<revs> * 360.0 / #<steps>]
    #<i>     = 0
    #<yy>    = #<ya>
    #<bb>    = 0
    o110 while [#<i> LT #<steps>]
      #<yy> = [#<yy> + #<dy>]
      #<bb> = [#<bb> + #<db>]
      G1 Y[#<yy>] B[#<bb>] F[#<feed>]
      #<i> = [#<i> + 1]
    o110 endwhile
    G0 Z[#<zsafe>]
  o100 endwhile

  G0 Y[#<ya>]
  G0 G53 Z0
  M5
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE DONE: #<pass> passes, stock now #<rf_dend> mm over #<rf_len> of length.)
o<rotary_face> endsub
M2 (end program)
